+  // -- Safe RPC method discovery for the standalone `-stdio` launcher -----
+  //
+  // lsp4j's default reflective RPC-method discovery
+  // (`ServiceEndpoints.getSupportedMethods`/`GenericEndpoint`, used by
+  // `org.eclipse.lsp4j.jsonrpc.Launcher.Builder`) scans `server.getClass()`.
+  // dotc's Mixin phase materializes a concrete forwarder on
+  // `DottyLanguageServer` for *every* default method it inherits from
+  // `LanguageServer`/`TextDocumentService`/`WorkspaceService` -- not just
+  // the ones this class overrides -- and each forwarder still carries the
+  // original `@JsonNotification`/`@JsonRequest` annotation. So the same RPC
+  // method ends up declared twice (once on the interface, once as dotc's
+  // forwarder on the class), and lsp4j's scanner isn't dedup-aware: it
+  // throws "Duplicate RPC method X." the first time this happens (e.g. for
+  // `initialized`, `codeAction`, `formatting`, ... -- anything with a
+  // default body this class doesn't override). Plain Java implementers
+  // never hit this, since javac doesn't synthesize forwarders for
+  // un-overridden default methods.
+  //
